WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.668
Thank you so much for being
here. Congrats on this show.

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.837
-Thank you. Thank you so much.
-So you -- In the first episode,

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
you play sort of
an acting teacher at a school.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:07.574 line:92%
You run the theater program.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:10.043
And you have to take a back seat
in the first episode

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:13.079
because a new acting teacher
comes in, played by Josh Radnor.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I-I -- My character,
Tracey Wolfe,

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:20.620 size:88% position:44%
has been working at that
high school for 20 years

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.188 line:92%
as the assistant drama director

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:25.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
and has been waiting for
the drama director

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
to either die or retire...
-Uh-huh. [ Laughs ]

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...so she can take the job.
And the woman retires,

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:34.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she gets passed over
for Josh Radnor's character.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when the show premiered
last week,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was so much
on social media.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.275 line:92%
People were so upset, you know,

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:46.746
and I feel that it was good that
they were upset, you know.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.749 size:78% position:39%
This show was written
prior to Time's Up.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.985 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But Time's Up is here.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was really happy that
people were so angry about it.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:01.161
And I think that when they
continue to watch the series,

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:04.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're gonna see Tracey
really stick up for herself,

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:07.734 size:78% position:39%
because in real life,
it doesn't happen,

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.169 line:92%
somebody tells somebody off

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then they get
the right position.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.840
It doesn't happen that way.
Real life is a lot messier.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.911
And most people can't just quit
their job and find another one.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Or tell off the principal

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
and still retain their job
and their position.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, you know,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.251 line:92%
I was actually really happy.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was happy that people were
pissed off.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.490
I'd be pissed off if you got...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.391 line:92%
if you got overlooked as well.

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:35.528
And you -- you pulled a lot
of your past to play Tracey,

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.932
because you started -- What is
it, the Urban Arts Partnership?

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.033 line:92%
Is that your organization?

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.801 line:92%
-Yes, I started -- I co-founded

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
Urban Arts Partnership
25 years ago.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.005 line:92%
We're an arts ed charity,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we service
only Title I schools.

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:51.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
That means schools at or below
the poverty line.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we go directly inside
the schools

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.148 line:92%
and we work with the principals.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
We review
the academic curricula.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have our programs.
Our programs have the students

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
help them comprehend
the academics.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's not just
art for art's sake.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.226 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's arts for education.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I've been doing this
for 25 years.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get this script and I just
started crying,

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.466
and my husband was like,
"What -- what's wrong now?"

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You know? [ Laughs ]

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- and I said,
"I can't believe that

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
my personal life is meeting
my professional life."

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's wonderful.
-"This is gonna be a breeze."

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember
I told my manager, I said,

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.780
"Call NBC and say this is mine."
[ Snapping fingers ]

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"This is mine."

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I'm glad it worked out.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Now, you... [ Clears throat ]

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:37.157
you were a beneficiary of people
who sort of reached out

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
and were helpful as well
when you were young.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:42.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You -- you learned to dance

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
and play baseball...
-Yeah.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.165 line:92%
-True story -- from nuns.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's correct.
-Wow.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:50.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah. I was --
I was a ward of the state.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:52.505 line:92%
And I was also in foster care.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
But prior to getting into
foster care,

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in
a Catholic home for children.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the nuns,
first day they were like,

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.413 line:92%
"You need to be on the stage."

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:03.216
And I was like, "No, I don't."
You know, I was a little kid.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:07.720
And they kept forcing the issue.
And they taught me how to tap.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
They taught me --
Well, they taught me ballet,

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they wouldn't let me be
in the ballet recitals

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.360
'cause they said I was too short
and my thighs were too chunky.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. Well. that's...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:16.563 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.531 size:88% position:44%
-That doesn't seem like
a very nun thing so say.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, but the best thing
they did was, um,

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.571 line:92%
teach me how to play baseball

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I ended up being
on the Little League,

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
girl's Little League.
-And I would not have believed

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.009 size:84% position:42%
that nuns taught people
how to play baseball,

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:33.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you brought this photo,
and that is proof right there.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:37.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is nothing
if not a nun playing baseball.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

